 "transcript": {
  "answer": "You're paying about **13.5% more for petrol than a year ago**, based on the ABS monthly CPI for **August 2026**, the latest data available.\n\n**What that means for a tank:** if a fill cost you $80 in August 2025, the same fill was about $91 in August 2026, roughly $11 more.\n\n**Prices have jumped around a lot this year.** Here's the year-on-year change in fuel prices:\n- Feb 2026: −7.2%\n- **Mar 2026: +24.2%** (the peak)\n- Apr 2026: +18.6%\n- May 2026: +7.7%\n- Jun 2026: −7.3%\n- Jul 2026: −0.4%\n- **Aug 2026: +13.5%**\n\nPrices briefly dropped below year-earlier levels in mid-2026, then rose sharply again in August.\n\n**Compared with prices overall:** all prices (headline inflation) rose 4.0% over the same year, so fuel went up more than three times as fast. That's why it's hurting.\n\nThese are national averages across the capital cities. What you pay at your local servo can differ, especially with weekly price cycles in some cities.",
